+def _refused_for_wave(cfg: Config, d: Path, trial: _AcceptTrial) -> bool:
+    """Whether bundle ``d``'s accept is refused because its change would conflict with
+    bundles of its own wave already accepted (#395) — refused as C6 refuses one: an open §6
+    row, the bundle left AWAITING_SIGNOFF, so no PR of it is opened beside theirs.
+
+    "Would conflict" is the fold's own rule, in the fold's order, on the commits publish
+    would push (:func:`integrate.same_wave_clash`): accepting ``d`` would make the fold after
+    the wave hold more bundles than it holds without it. So whichever bundle is accepted
+    first is kept, and the accepted bundles of a wave hold no such conflict unless the human
+    overrides. When that check cannot run for ``d``'s target (a lock, a fetch, a commit
+    that cannot be built), ``d`` is refused only if its patch may share a path with an
+    accepted bundle of the wave on that target (:func:`integrate.same_wave_overlap`), as a
+    textual conflict needs one: a shared path, or a patch whose paths cannot all be read,
+    which may share any. Otherwise it is accepted, and stderr says so. A check that left the
+    shared integration worktree in a state it could not put back is not that: the fold
+    stops on the same errors (:class:`integrate.IntegrationTreeError`, #631;
+    :class:`integrate._LineBroken`, #623), so ``d`` is refused whatever it shares, with a row
+    that names the tree's state and the step for it — never accepted on a broken tree.
+
+    The row names the bundles it conflicts with, the files, and the step: declare
+    ``Conflicts with`` in ``d``'s brief (the partners it does not declare yet), then
+    iterate-plan — which the next run re-plans, not this one (:func:`_hold_replan`). It goes
+    into SUMMARY §6 only (:func:`signoff.ensure_needs_human_item`), never into a Check
+    artifact, so a SUMMARY reassembled later drops it and the next accept tries again. A
+    row already there and ticked is the human's override, as C6 honours every tick: the
+    accept goes on, and the fold holds one of the two (#674). Each refusal is recorded in
+    ``state.SAME_WAVE_REFUSAL`` for :func:`_drive_wave`, which offers the bundle one more
+    sign-off session, not one every pass."""
